IMPORT prelude

-- Regulation of Imports and Exports Act 1995 (Singapore) -- what counts as an import or export and as "goods" (s 2); the
-- penalty ceilings for breach of the trade regulations and for the trade-information-certificate and trade-description offences
-- (ss 3(3), 10A, 10E, 10F, 10G, 10H, 28A) and for the other offences in the Act (ss 7, 11, 16, 17, 19, 27, 28, 29, 30, 31);
-- self-issued preferential certificates of origin (s 10H); surrender of cancelled permits (s 7); the authorised-issuer
-- regulatory-action procedure (s 10D); reporting a seizure (s 13(2)); examination costs (s 20(3)); liability for agents and
-- employees (s 36(4)); composition (s 39); and appeal to the Minister (s 39A).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/RIEA1995.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 16 of 2026 (in force 30 September 2026) shown; Part 3 (trade information certificates) as inserted or substituted by
-- Act 26 of 2025 with effect from 29 September 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a trader, a certificate
-- issuer or their adviser meets. Not encoded: the regulation-making powers themselves (s 3(2), 8(11), 10I) -- the actual import and
-- export controls live in regulations, which were not retrieved; the computer service and its evidential presumptions (s 8);
-- service of notices (s 9); search, seizure, arrest and computer-inspection powers (ss 12, 14-26); disclosure gateways in s 31(1)
-- beyond the offence; informers (s 37); cross-border railway preclearance (s 39AA); and Part 6.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Regulation of Imports and Exports Act 1995 -- offences and trader rules`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `2 -- import, export and goods`

-- s 2: "import" means to bring into Singapore from outside "but does not include the bringing into Singapore of goods which are to
-- be taken out of Singapore on the same conveyance on which they were brought into Singapore without any landing or transhipment
-- within Singapore". "export" means to take out of Singapore, and includes placing goods in a conveyance to be taken out, "but does
-- not include the taking out from Singapore of any goods on the same conveyance on which they were brought into Singapore unless
-- such goods ... have been landed or transhipped within Singapore".
GIVEN `brought into Singapore from outside` IS A BOOLEAN, `leaves on the same conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN, `landed or transhipped in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an import` IF
    `brought into Singapore from outside` AND ((NOT `leaves on the same conveyance`) OR `landed or transhipped in Singapore`)

GIVEN `taken out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `on the conveyance it arrived on` IS A BOOLEAN, `landed or transhipped in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an export` IF
    `taken out of Singapore` AND ((NOT `on the conveyance it arrived on`) OR `landed or transhipped in Singapore`)

-- s 2: "goods" means any movable or personal property "but does not include choses in action and money (except for a collector's
-- piece, an investment article or item of numismatic interest and currency notes imported or exported in substantial quantities)".
DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `a container of machine parts`
    `a debt or other chose in action`
    `ordinary banknotes in a wallet`
    `a collector's coin`
    `an investment gold bar`
    `currency notes in substantial quantities`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is goods` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `a debt or other chose in action` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `ordinary banknotes in a wallet` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(3), 7, 10A, 10E-10H, 11, 16, 17, 19, 27-31 -- penalty ceilings`

-- Value-linked ceiling, used by s 3(3) (what regulations may provide), s 10A(6), s 10F(2), s 10G(3) and (4) and s 28A(1): first
-- offence "a fine not exceeding $100,000 or 3 times the value of the goods ..., whichever is the greater, or ... imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 2 years or ... both"; second or subsequent offence "$200,000 or 4 times the value", 3 years. For s 10G(2) the
-- value is that of "goods Y", the goods the certificate is falsely said to cover.
-- s 10E: an authorised certificate issuer who issues a certificate it "knows or ought reasonably to know is false or misleading" --
-- $10,000 or 2 years. s 10H(5): a self-issuing manufacturer or exporter who keeps no records, defies a records requirement or
-- issues a false preferential certificate -- $100,000 or 2 years; $200,000 or 3 years (no value multiplier).
-- s 7(4) failing to surrender a cancelled or suspended permit -- $3,000. s 11(2) failing to produce a licence, permit or trade
-- information certificate -- $3,000. s 16(7) conveyance directions -- $6,000 or 12 months. s 17(3) tampering with an officer's lock
-- or seal -- $6,000 or 6 months. s 19(2) failing to remove goods to an examination station when required -- $6,000. s 27
-- obstruction or destroying records -- $15,000 or 12 months. s 28 false declarations -- $10,000 or 2 years. s 29 computer
-- manipulation to evade controls -- $10,000 or 2 years. s 30(4) failing to furnish information -- $6,000 or 6 months. s 31(6), (7)
-- unlawful disclosure -- $6,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `breaching the import and export regulations`
    `issuing a certificate posing as an authorised issuer`
    `tampering with a trade information certificate`
    `misrepresenting who issued a certificate`
    `misrepresenting which goods a certificate covers`
    `applying an incorrect trade description`
    `an authorised issuer issuing a false certificate`
    `a self-issuer breaching section 10H`
    `making a false declaration`
    `manipulating a computer to evade controls`
    `obstructing an officer`
    `failing to surrender a cancelled permit`
    `failing to produce a permit or certificate`
    `defying a conveyance direction`
    `tampering with an officer's seal`
    `failing to remove goods when required`
    `failing to furnish information`
    `unlawfully disclosing trade information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is linked to the value of the goods` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breaching the import and export regulations` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `issuing a certificate posing as an authorised issuer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `tampering with a trade information certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `misrepresenting who issued a certificate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `misrepresenting which goods a certificate covers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `applying an incorrect trade description` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fixed fine ceiling` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an authorised issuer issuing a false certificate` THEN 10000
    WHEN `making a false declaration` THEN 10000
    WHEN `manipulating a computer to evade controls` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 15000
    WHEN `failing to surrender a cancelled permit` THEN 3000
    WHEN `failing to produce a permit or certificate` THEN 3000
    WHEN `defying a conveyance direction` THEN 6000
    WHEN `tampering with an officer's seal` THEN 6000
    WHEN `failing to remove goods when required` THEN 6000
    WHEN `failing to furnish information` THEN 6000
    WHEN `unlawfully disclosing trade information` THEN 6000
    OTHERWISE IF `repeat` THEN 200000 ELSE 100000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `value of the goods` IS A NUMBER, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the fine is linked to the value of the goods` `the offence`
    THEN IF `repeat`
         THEN `the greater of` 200000 (4 TIMES `value of the goods`)
         ELSE `the greater of` 100000 (3 TIMES `value of the goods`)
    ELSE `the fixed fine ceiling` `the offence` `repeat`

-- Imprisonment ceiling in months; 0 where the section provides a fine only (ss 7(4), 11(2), 19(2)).
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `an authorised issuer issuing a false certificate` THEN 24
    WHEN `making a false declaration` THEN 24
    WHEN `manipulating a computer to evade controls` THEN 24
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to surrender a cancelled permit` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to produce a permit or certificate` THEN 0
    WHEN `defying a conveyance direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `tampering with an officer's seal` THEN 6
    WHEN `failing to remove goods when required` THEN 0
    WHEN `failing to furnish information` THEN 6
    WHEN `unlawfully disclosing trade information` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE IF `repeat` THEN 36 ELSE 24

§§ `10A(4), (5) and 10H -- who may issue a certificate`

-- s 10A(4): a person "must not issue any trade information certificate ... as an authorised certificate issuer for that class ...
-- unless the person is in fact such authorised certificate issuer". (5): (4) does not apply to a person who does not issue it
-- "(whether expressly or by implication) as an authorised certificate issuer".
GIVEN `holds out as an authorised issuer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is authorised for that class of certificate and goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `issuing the certificate breaches section 10A(4)` IF
    `holds out as an authorised issuer` AND (NOT `is authorised for that class of certificate and goods`)

-- s 10H(1): nothing in Part 3 prevents a manufacturer or exporter (Z) from issuing "on Z's own account, in respect of any of Z's
-- goods for export or re-export", a preferential certificate of origin if (a) the preferential tariff arrangement with the
-- destination "permits the issue ... by Z"; (b) it is in a form and manner acceptable to the destination; and (c) Z does not issue
-- it as an authorised certificate issuer.
GIVEN `the agreement with the destination permits self-certification` IS A BOOLEAN, `the form is acceptable to the destination` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds out as an authorised issuer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exporter may self-issue the preferential certificate` IF
        `the agreement with the destination permits self-certification`
    AND `the form is acceptable to the destination`
    AND (NOT `holds out as an authorised issuer`)

§§ `7(2)-(4) -- surrendering a cancelled permit`

-- s 7(2): if a certificate, licence or permit "is cancelled or suspended, the holder ... must, unless it has otherwise been lawfully
-- disposed of, surrender it forthwith". (3): "Subsection (2) does not apply to a certificate, licence or permit issued by an
-- electronic notice".
GIVEN `cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `lawfully disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN, `issued by electronic notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder must surrender it` IF
    `cancelled or suspended` AND (NOT `lawfully disposed of`) AND (NOT `issued by electronic notice`)

§§ `10D -- cancelling or suspending an authorised issuer`

-- s 10D(1): the Director-General may cancel, "or suspend for a period not exceeding 6 months", an authorisation if satisfied of
-- (a) fraud or misrepresentation, (b) breach of a condition or of the Act or regulations, or (c) the issuer is no longer fit and
-- proper. (2), (3): before acting, a written notice giving at least 14 days for representations.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `obtained by fraud or misrepresentation`
    `breach of a condition`
    `breach of the Act or regulations`
    `no longer fit and proper`
    `commercial rivalry`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground supports regulatory action` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `commercial rivalry` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `is a suspension` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER, `days given for representations` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulatory action is within section 10D` IF
        `the ground supports regulatory action` `the ground`
    AND `days given for representations` AT LEAST 14
    AND ((NOT `is a suspension`) OR `months of suspension` AT MOST 6)

§§ `13(2) -- reporting a seizure`

-- s 13(2): the Director-General "must, within one month from the date of the seizure, (unless a prosecution has before the expiry
-- of that period been commenced and is pending ...) report the fact of the seizure to a District Court".
GIVEN `a month has passed since seizure` IS A BOOLEAN, `reported to a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN, `prosecution commenced and pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seizure report is overdue` IF
    `a month has passed since seizure` AND (NOT `reported to a District Court`) AND (NOT `prosecution commenced and pending`)

§§ `20(3) -- who pays for bringing a package to be examined`

-- s 20(3): the cost "must be borne by the importer or exporter if the particulars, information or documents furnished (or any of
-- them) are found to be substantially inaccurate".
GIVEN `found substantially inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trader bears the examination cost` IF `found substantially inaccurate`

§§ `28 -- false declarations`

-- s 28(1): a person who, being required to make a declaration or produce a document, or for the purpose of obtaining a
-- certificate, licence or permit, makes a declaration "false in a material particular" or produces a false, unauthentic or
-- tampered document, is guilty "unless he or she proves that he or she had taken all reasonable steps to ascertain ... the truth
-- and genuineness thereof".
GIVEN `required or seeking a permit` IS A BOOLEAN, `false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all reasonable steps` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false declaration is an offence` IF
    `required or seeking a permit` AND `false in a material particular` AND (NOT `proved all reasonable steps`)

§§ `28A -- incorrect trade descriptions`

-- s 28A(6): "trade description" is one that "relates to the place of origin, manufacture or production of the goods". (1): the
-- offence is committed by "Any person who imports, exports or tranships any goods" and applies an incorrect trade description or
-- has such goods for sale or trade. (3): for goods bound for a country with a prescribed agreement, a description "is treated as
-- being incorrect if it is not in accordance with any rules of origin specified in that agreement".
GIVEN `imports exports or tranships` IS A BOOLEAN, `the description concerns origin or manufacture` IS A BOOLEAN, `the description is incorrect` IS A BOOLEAN, `bound for a prescribed-agreement country` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets that agreement's rules of origin` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trade description offence is made out` IF
        `imports exports or tranships`
    AND `the description concerns origin or manufacture`
    AND (    `the description is incorrect`
          OR (`bound for a prescribed-agreement country` AND (NOT `meets that agreement's rules of origin`)))

§§ `36(4) -- acts of partners, agents and employees`

-- s 36(4): a person is guilty of an offence done by the person's partner, agent or employee in the course of the business or
-- employment "unless the person proves ... that the offence was committed without the person's knowledge and that the person took
-- all reasonable precautions to prevent that act or omission". Both limbs.
GIVEN `done by partner agent or employee in the course of business` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved without knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable for the act` IF
    `done by partner agent or employee in the course of business` AND (NOT (`proved without knowledge` AND `proved all reasonable precautions`))

§§ `39 -- composition`

-- s 39(1): a senior authorised officer may compound an offence "which is prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting a sum
-- not exceeding "(a) $1,000 in respect of any offence where the maximum fine prescribed for that offence is less than $5,000; and
-- (b) $5,000 in respect of any other prescribed offence". The list of compoundable offences is in regulations (not retrieved), so
-- this computes only the ceiling IF an offence is prescribed.
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling for a maximum fine of` MEANS
    IF `maximum fine` LESS THAN 5000 THEN 1000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `value of the goods` IS A NUMBER, `repeat` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling` MEANS
    `the composition ceiling for a maximum fine of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` `value of the goods` `repeat`)

§§ `39A -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 39A(2): an appeal "must be made in writing within 14 days after the date the decision appealed against is served, and must
-- provide adequate details of the grounds". (3): the Minister "may reject" a non-compliant appeal. (5): the decision is final.
-- (7): "Unless the Minister directs otherwise", an appeal does not affect the operation of the decision.
GIVEN `days after service` IS A NUMBER, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `gives adequate grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal complies with section 39A(2)` IF
    `days after service` AT MOST 14 AND `in writing` AND `gives adequate grounds`

GIVEN `the Minister directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision must be complied with pending the appeal` IF
    NOT `the Minister directs otherwise`
